---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { profile } from '../../data/site';
import { personId, personSchema, websiteId, websiteSchema } from '../../lib/identity';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/paths';

const root = Astro.site ?? new URL('https://sangtruong.me');
const canonical = new URL(withBase('/work/yhct'), root).href;
const jsonLd = [
  personSchema(root),
  websiteSchema(root),
  {
    '@type': 'CreativeWork',
    '@id': `${canonical}#case-study`,
    url: canonical,
    name: 'Clinical AI & Decision Support — Sang Truong',
    description: 'Public, intentionally bounded case study of a clinician-facing AI decision-support platform built under EPIC TECHNOLOGY.',
    author: { '@id': personId(root) },
    isPartOf: { '@id': websiteId(root) },
    inLanguage: 'en',
    dateModified: '2026-09-11T21:14:00+07:00',
  },
];

const layers = [
  ['01', 'Clinical workflow', 'Questions, medication and herbal workflows, prescription review, follow-up context.'],
  ['02', 'AI reasoning', 'Language understanding and synthesis operate inside bounded application contracts.'],
  ['03', 'Evidence & authority', 'Governed knowledge, citations, deterministic facts, permissions, and durable state stay explicit.'],
  ['04', 'Delivery boundary', 'Validation, failure behavior, deployment constraints, and human use are treated as engineering concerns.'],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Clinical AI & Decision Support | Sang Truong"
  description="A public, deliberately abstracted case study of Sang Truong's clinician-facing clinical AI and decision-support work under EPIC TECHNOLOGY."
  image="og-yhct.png"
  imageAlt="Clinical AI case study by Sang Truong"
  pageType="article"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="case container">
    <a class="back-link" href={withBase('/#work')}>← Flagship systems</a>

    <header class="case-hero safe-case-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Clinical AI · EPIC TECHNOLOGY</p>
      <h1>AI that can reason without becoming the source of truth.</h1>
      <p class="case-lede">I architected and built a clinician-facing AI platform for Ho Chi Minh City Traditional Medicine Hospital. The interesting part is not the chat box — it is keeping reasoning, evidence, clinical authority, state, failure behavior, and deployment constraints from collapsing into one opaque model call.</p>
      <div class="case-meta">
        <div><span>Role</span><strong>AI Architect / Lead Builder</strong></div>
        <div><span>Setting</span><strong>Hospital clinical workflows</strong></div>
        <div><span>Public scope</span><strong>Architecture boundary only</strong></div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="case-section section-rule safe-split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The engineering problem</p>
        <h2>A useful answer is not automatically a safe system.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose-stack">
        <p>The product has to understand natural language and synthesize useful responses, while application-owned facts, source provenance, permissions, conversation state, and clinical constraints remain independently inspectable.</p>
        <p>I designed the system so AI reasoning can be flexible where it helps, but it cannot silently redefine authoritative knowledge or erase uncertainty when a dependency fails.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule">
      <div class="section-heading compact-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Public system cut</p><h2>Four layers. Clear authority.</h2></div>
        <p class="section-note">This is intentionally not the deployment diagram. It shows what each layer is responsible for, without publishing private corpus structure, prompts, provider configuration, infrastructure topology, or operational controls.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="safe-architecture">
        {layers.map(([index, title, detail]) => (
          <article>
            <span>{index}</span>
            <div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{detail}</p></div>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule safe-split">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">What I owned</p><h2>From ambiguous requirement to acceptance boundary.</h2></div>
      <div class="decision-list">
        <article><strong>System semantics.</strong><p>Defined where language-model reasoning ends and application/source authority begins.</p></article>
        <article><strong>Product & backend path.</strong><p>Built the clinician-facing workflow, APIs, durable state, retrieval/evidence path, permissions, and streaming behavior.</p></article>
        <article><strong>Failure design.</strong><p>Kept dependency and provider failures explicit rather than converting them into plausible-looking clinical output.</p></article>
        <article><strong>Delivery.</strong><p>Designed around on-premise constraints, testability, observability, provider portability, and clinician-facing acceptance.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule privacy-panel">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Deliberately withheld</p>
        <h2>The public case study stops before the sensitive layer.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Private clinical corpus details, prompt/system instructions, internal schemas, credentials, deployment topology, machine identities, release artifacts, runbooks, clinician data, and exact operational controls are not published. The goal is to demonstrate engineering judgment — not ship a map of the hospital system.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule principle-panel">
      <blockquote>The model may own synthesis. It should not silently own truth, permission, or evidence.</blockquote>
      <p class="muted">That boundary is the reusable part of this project: it applies to any high-consequence AI product where a fluent answer is weaker evidence than the system state behind it.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule case-cta">
      <p class="eyebrow">Explore more</p>
      <h2>The résumé carries the breadth. This page carries the boundary.</h2>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href={withBase('/yhct')}>Giải thích tiếng Việt</a><a class="button ghost" href={withBase('/resume')}>Full résumé</a><a class="button ghost" href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>Contact</a></div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .safe-case-hero h1 { max-width: 12ch; }
  .safe-split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .85fr 1.15fr; gap: clamp(40px, 8vw, 100px); align-items: start; }
  .prose-stack p { margin-top: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .safe-architecture { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .safe-architecture article { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 72px 1fr; gap: 24px; padding: 28px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .safe-architecture article > span { color: var(--accent); font: 650 .78rem/1 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }
  .safe-architecture h3 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vw, 2rem); letter-spacing: -.035em; }
  .safe-architecture p { margin: 0; max-width: 68ch; color: var(--muted); }
  .privacy-panel { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .8fr 1.2fr; gap: clamp(36px, 8vw, 110px); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface) 94%, var(--accent)); padding-inline: clamp(24px, 5vw, 64px); border-left: 1px solid var(--line); border-right: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .privacy-panel p:last-child { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.02rem; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .safe-split, .privacy-panel { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
